{"title":"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An ice cream <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cone\" title=\"Cone\">cone</a> consists of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sphere\" title=\"Sphere\">sphere</a> of vanilla ice cream and a right circular cone that has the same diameter as the sphere. If the ice cream melts, it will exactly fill the cone. Assume that the melted ice cream occupies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e126f0d41c904d37ba2c332347a24b75d4ac3066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$75\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the volume of the frozen ice cream. What is the ratio of the cone’s height to its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a>? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/9/e19ae8da3923f3880ba56d7e59f3c8b2e0e55648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 2:1 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 3:1 \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 4:1 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 16:3 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 6:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"472\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the common radius of the sphere and the cone, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the cone’s height. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abe59fc13b9d7b3ab5893c9a287df3ce7ff21e74.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[75\\% \\cdot \\left(\\frac 43 \\pi r^3\\right) = \\frac 13 \\pi r^2 h \\Longrightarrow h = 3r\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"43\" />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f4456ebd12d3a61b959b0cb63b61d6ddca0b19c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h:r = 3:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B\">2003 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by